<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:05:18 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Russian strikes on Ukraine’s Zaporizhzhia kill two people and wound dozens more</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-live-tripoli-demands-explanation-from-kyiv-for-striking-russian-ships-in-libyan-waters</link><description>
A Russian attack killed two people in the Ukrainian city of Zaporizhzhia overnight, regional governor Mykhailo Semikin said on Tuesday. Some 40 people, four of them children, were also wounded in the strikes, the governor added. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d0cbce6-e7dc-11f1-bf71-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26328267479822.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d0cbce6-e7dc-11f1-bf71-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26328267479822.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4eef989e-e7b9-11f1-9771-2fc327d3c693</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 05:50:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d0cbce6-e7dc-11f1-bf71-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26328267479822.jpg">© Ukrainian Emergency Service via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky urges four-way peace talks with Russia, Europe and US 'as soon as possible'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-zelensky-urges-four-way-peace-talks-with-russia-europe-and-us-as-soon-as-possible</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky is calling for a new round of negotiations involving Ukraine, Russia, the United States and European leaders, saying Kyiv is ready to meet as early as Tuesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3999d8f4-e21b-11f1-8b8b-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316805802362.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3999d8f4-e21b-11f1-8b8b-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316805802362.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">35bca120-e79e-11f1-a59f-11cafe6bee07</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:30:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3999d8f4-e21b-11f1-8b8b-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316805802362.jpg">© Peter Morrison, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>NATO vows space defence after Russia nuclear satellite report</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nato-vows-space-defence-after-russia-nuclear-satellite-report</link><description>
NATO chief Mark Rutte said Monday the alliance would defend against threats in space when asked about German media reports that Russia may be preparing to launch a nuclear-armed satellite. The media reports, citing unnamed German military and BND spy agency sources, said Moscow was thought to be planning such a launch in the coming weeks, giving it the capability to destroy other satellites. FRANCE 24's Laurent Berstecher reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f1e3dc6-e78d-11f1-9ce0-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-230634-230830-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f1e3dc6-e78d-11f1-9ce0-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-230634-230830-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34db6a54-e78d-11f1-88d8-870f7a08acc9</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:33:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'A war of unmanned machines, AI and total transparency of the battlefield'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield</link><description>
Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that today's war in Ukraine "is a war of unmanned machines, AI, total transparency of the battlefield, mass drones attacks and long range weapons, and this means we have to rethink how to protect human beings".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fcfa0244-e787-11f1-ae27-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-223115-224132-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fcfa0244-e787-11f1-ae27-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-223115-224132-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0302153c-e788-11f1-8d6c-fb9e050d4e4d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:54:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Libya's east seeks UN probe into claims Ukrainian military present in west</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/libya-s-east-seeks-un-probe-into-claims-ukrainian-military-present-in-west</link><description>
Authorities in divided Libya's east called on Monday for the United Nations to investigate claims that Ukrainian forces were present in the country's west, as they lodged a complaint over Ukrainian attacks on two Russian ships off Benghazi. The strikes on Sunday, claimed by Kyiv, come as Ukraine steps up strikes against Russia far from the front lines of their war. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a90c2d3e-e777-11f1-bbf4-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-203823-204018-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a90c2d3e-e777-11f1-bbf4-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-203823-204018-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aea6fa9e-e777-11f1-9474-fb9e58ec7684</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:08:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine claims it sank Russian warship off Libya</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-claims-it-sank-russian-warship-off-libya</link><description>
Ukraine on Monday claimed it was behind strikes on two Russian vessels off Libya, including one that sank a modern warship, in the latest spillover from Moscow's invasion. The attacks on Sunday near the Libyan port of Benghazi come at a time when Ukraine has stepped up its daring strikes against Russia far from the frontlines in retaliation for Moscow's deadly invasion. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42bcf66a-e774-11f1-99b6-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-201152-201640-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42bcf66a-e774-11f1-99b6-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-201152-201640-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48b7cbee-e774-11f1-b0d7-bfc2d1688614</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:39:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Finland summons Russian ambassador after suspected airspace violation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-finland-summons-russian-ambassador-after-suspected-airspace-violation</link><description>
Finland on Monday said it had summoned Russia's ambassador over a suspected violation of Finnish airspace by a Russian helicopter and after a Ukrainian drone strike on a Russian cargo ship located in the Gulf of Finland in recent days. Helsinki also condemned Moscow's escalating strikes on civilian targets in Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ad57222-e759-11f1-9bc1-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326490305591.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ad57222-e759-11f1-9bc1-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326490305591.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">54a67868-e758-11f1-86b6-1b6ab457b0a3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:50:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ad57222-e759-11f1-9bc1-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326490305591.jpg">© Finnish Border Guard/Lehtikuva via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>12,000 evacuated from Don Toliver concert after unknown substance sickens fans</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-12-000-evacuated-from-don-toliver-concert-after-unknown-substance-sickens-fans</link><description>
More than 12,000 fans were evacuated from a concert by American rapper Don Toliver and over 80 were treated by medics after an unknown irritant was released in the crowd, authorities in the English city of Manchester said Monday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1342f74c-e754-11f1-9e59-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/minimanchester.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1342f74c-e754-11f1-9e59-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/minimanchester.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29a5c636-e754-11f1-b238-4b6329e1cde4</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:46:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine claims strikes on Russian ships off Libyan coast</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-ukraine-claims-strikes-on-russian-ships-off-libyan-coast</link><description>
Ukraine claimed responsibility on Monday for attacks on two Russian vessels off the coast of Libya the previous day. Here is what we know about the operation, claimed by President Volodymyr Zelensky shortly after the United Nations called for an investigation into the strikes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b333898c-e746-11f1-aae4-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/miniukraine-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b333898c-e746-11f1-aae4-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/miniukraine-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b99b296a-e746-11f1-907d-f78eb5920847</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:36:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Libya demands answers from Kyiv over drone attack on Russian ships off Benghazi</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-live-russian-strikes-kill-at-least-15-people-in-kyiv-region-ukraine-says</link><description>
Libya's Tripoli-based government on Monday condemned Ukraine's strikes on two Russian vessels near the eastern city of Benghazi carried out by Ukraine on Sunday. It demanded an explanation from Kyiv, warning that Libya would not be dragged into the war between Russia and Ukraine. Read our live blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2beb690a-e763-11f1-9f1c-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T165345Z-506739161-RC2KTOAEVHGN-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-SHIPS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2beb690a-e763-11f1-9f1c-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T165345Z-506739161-RC2KTOAEVHGN-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-SHIPS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">54b63f42-e702-11f1-bbd8-bb74ee9238c2</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:10:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2beb690a-e763-11f1-9f1c-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T165345Z-506739161-RC2KTOAEVHGN-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-SHIPS.jpg">© Vantor via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA[Burnham, 'Brejoin' & the ghosts of Brexit]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261122-burnham-brejoin-the-ghosts-of-brexit</link><description>
"The people of Britain have spoken, and the answer is: we are out." Those were the words of David Dimbleby at 4:40am on June 24, 2016, as the Brexit referendum result became clear. But nearly a decade on, is Britain changing its mind? Prime Minister Andy Burnham has reopened talks with Brussels, exploring options for a closer relationship with the EU. The move has, however, drawn criticism from key figures behind Brexit, including Theresa May and Boris Johnson. What is driving this rethink and where might it lead? FRANCE 24's Gavin Lee speaks to John McTernan, veteran Labour strategist and former adviser to Tony Blair.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2630c73e-e764-11f1-8e96-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/0d8dfe91-6904-423b-a52a-61ad0da8e85b.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2630c73e-e764-11f1-8e96-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/0d8dfe91-6904-423b-a52a-61ad0da8e85b.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e32e232-e6ac-11f1-91aa-09eb8656efc7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:37:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Europe sees new protests over rising costs, inequality and public services</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe-sees-new-protests-over-rising-costs-inequality-and-public-services</link><description>
Sunday marks the third consecutive day of protests across Europe, following large demonstrations on Friday and smaller rallies on Saturday, from Portugal to France. The protests have largely focused on the rising cost of living and access to affordable housing. In France, demonstrations have now taken place for six weekends in a row. Ophelie Jacobson reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53de5938-e658-11f1-9f3b-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-100542-100715-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53de5938-e658-11f1-9f3b-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-100542-100715-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">59a45386-e658-11f1-a12d-1b55d91421ae</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:41:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukrainian rescuers search for survivors in rubble after Russian attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261122-live-finland-says-war-spilling-over-after-baltic-sea-drone-strike-on-russian-cargo-ship</link><description>
Ukrainian rescue teams on Sunday searched for survivors in the rubble of a collapsed residential building in Dymer, in the Kyiv region, after a Russian drone strike, which killed two people and wounded four others. Meanwhile, Finland warned the war was "spilling over" after a drone set fire to a Russian cargo ship in the Baltic Sea Saturday. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/91402a2e-e656-11f1-ad74-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-22T082023Z-1682293497-RC2WSOAB5T2M-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-REGION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/91402a2e-e656-11f1-ad74-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-22T082023Z-1682293497-RC2WSOAB5T2M-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-REGION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7894ceac-e639-11f1-9490-25047c8f4b46</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:15:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/91402a2e-e656-11f1-ad74-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-22T082023Z-1682293497-RC2WSOAB5T2M-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-REGION.jpg">© Thomas Peter, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU-Indonesia agreement sees the light after ten years of negotiations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261121-eu-indonesia-agreement-sees-the-light-after-ten-years-of-negotiations</link><description>
The European Union and Indonesia have signed a major trade deal, ten years after talks began.The agreement removes almost all tariffs between the EU and Southeast Asia's biggest economy: 98.5 per cent of them. For Europe, it means access to a market of 280 million people and a steadier supply of nickel for batteries. For Indonesia, easier exports of palm oil, textiles and footwear, and it arrives just before its current EU trade preferences end on the 1st of January. To discuss the deal Airlangga Hartarto, Coordinating Minister for Economic Affairs in Indonesia joined us on the programme. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea9d9328-e5f6-11f1-b921-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a5f225a1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea9d9328-e5f6-11f1-b921-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a5f225a1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">42bad4e0-e5f6-11f1-b300-9d257b5e701b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:23:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia attacks Zelensky's hometown, Ukraine reaffirms wish to join NATO</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-russia-attacks-zelensky-s-hometown-ukraine-reaffirms-wish-to-join-nato</link><description>
A Russian ballistic missile attack on President Volodymyr Zelensky’s hometown in central Ukraine on Saturday killed two people and wounded dozens. Hours later, Zelensky reiterated his country's determination to join NATO, following proposals to provide Kyiv with security guarantees similar to those of the military alliance.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/700b9322-e5d7-11f1-9865-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26325430245749.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/700b9322-e5d7-11f1-9865-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26325430245749.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf445f0e-e5d7-11f1-b974-8522af8c30e5</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:56:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/700b9322-e5d7-11f1-9865-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26325430245749.jpg">© AP via Dnipropetrovsk regional military</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia launches ballistic missile attack on Zelensky's hometown in central Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-launches-ballistic-missile-attack-on-zelensky-s-hometown-in-central-ukraine</link><description>
A Russian ballistic missile attack on President Volodymyr Zelensky’s hometown in central Ukraine on Saturday killed two people and wounded dozens. Hours later, Zelensky reiterated his country's determination to join NATO. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1864982-e5d3-11f1-8806-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-180653-181143-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1864982-e5d3-11f1-8806-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-180653-181143-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a6552e7e-e5d3-11f1-b5bc-5b53ef367d23</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:55:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Drone attack sets Russian cargo ship ablaze in Gulf of Finland</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland</link><description>
A Russian cargo ship caught fire after ​being hit by drones in the Baltic Sea on Saturday and drifted into Finnish waters. Reporting from Kyiv, FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg notes that the ship is affiliated with a major Russian military logistics company. While Ukrainian authorities typically neither confirm nor deny responsibility, analysts cite a clear motive for the targeting, Cragg explains. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8752a08e-e5d2-11f1-bad2-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-180424-180619-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8752a08e-e5d2-11f1-bad2-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-180424-180619-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8ce73186-e5d2-11f1-a09a-734ccf1eac6b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:02:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Drone attack sets Russian cargo ship ablaze in Gulf of Finland</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland</link><description>
A Russian cargo ship caught fire after a drone strike in international waters in the Gulf of Finland on Saturday and later drifted into the country's ⁠territorial waters, Finnish authorities said. Helsinki alerted NATO and imposed temporary restrictions in the area amid heightened tensions in the Baltic Sea.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c370820-e5d6-11f1-9a48-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26325640446049.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c370820-e5d6-11f1-9a48-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26325640446049.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">94f19a56-e5a5-11f1-bf66-3389c226a5ad</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:35:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c370820-e5d6-11f1-9a48-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26325640446049.jpg">© AP via Handout Lehtikuva/Finnish Border Guard</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'Accept cookies'? Russia collects data from swaths of unknowing Swedes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-accept-cookies-russia-collected-data-swaths-unknowing-swedes</link><description>
A Russian tech firm backed by an oligarch close to President Vladimir Putin has secretly been collecting data from hundreds of thousands – possibly millions – of Swedes, a newspaper investigation found. The revelation has rattled the Nordic nation, whose proximity to Russia and unusually open public records system make it particularly vulnerable to Moscow’s hybrid war tactics.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75dade0c-e500-11f1-86bd-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP21173406344763.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75dade0c-e500-11f1-86bd-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP21173406344763.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7189bb56-e4fc-11f1-aa36-c70dad960c65</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:55:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75dade0c-e500-11f1-86bd-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP21173406344763.jpg">© Photo illustration Jenny Kane, AP  </source><dc:creator>Louise NORDSTROM</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'Unacceptable': EU chief condemns alleged Russian plot to kill US-Ukrainian citizen</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-unacceptable-eu-chief-condemns-alleged-russian-plot-to-kill-us-ukrainian-citizen</link><description>
European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen condemned an alleged Russian intelligence plot to assassinate a US-Ukrainian citizen in Denmark, vowing full solidarity with Copenhagen.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09933754-e590-11f1-bdd0-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132245Z-1935520672-RC2OROAXK61L-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09933754-e590-11f1-bdd0-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132245Z-1935520672-RC2OROAXK61L-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5900437c-e590-11f1-b067-8332edeefda7</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:32:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09933754-e590-11f1-bdd0-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132245Z-1935520672-RC2OROAXK61L-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT.jpg">© Yves Herman, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU, UK reach reset deal after Brexit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/eu-uk-reach-reset-deal-after-brexit</link><description>
The UK and the EU signed three agreements on Friday at a summit in Brussels, marking a new effort to reset post-Brexit relations. The deals aim to reduce red tape for food exports, link emissions trading schemes and allow tens of thousands of young people to live and work more freely across the Channel. Prime Minister Andy Burnham has called Brexit an “obvious failure” to deliver on its promises and wants to deepen ties with the EU, a position criticised by veteran Brexiteer Nigel Farage, who has warned of a political backlash. Daniel Quinlan has this story.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9dec5f4-e58d-11f1-9664-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-091304-091457-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9dec5f4-e58d-11f1-9664-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-091304-091457-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bedc75f6-e58d-11f1-b084-57bea9daef2a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:43:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>UK and EU strike ‘landmark’ deal to rebuild ties after Brexit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-uk-and-eu-strike-landmark-deal-to-rebuild-ties-after-brexit</link><description>
🇬🇧🇪🇺 A fresh start after #Brexit? The #UK and #EU have agreed on a landmark #deal to rebuild ties, following a summit in Brussels this Friday. The agreement covers easier food export checks, youth mobility and carbon emission quotas.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c262fdc-e4ef-11f1-b8c1-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/burnham-00-00-07-21-Still001.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c262fdc-e4ef-11f1-b8c1-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/burnham-00-00-07-21-Still001.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d39d622-e4ef-11f1-9408-317a34d99d64</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:06:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>‘A more expensive EU is not a better EU’: Austria's Minister for Europe, Claudia Bauer</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-a-more-expensive-eu-is-not-a-better-eu-austria-s-minister-for-europe-claudia-bauer</link><description>
This week's programme hosted Claudia Bauer, Austria’s Federal Minister for Europe, Integration and Family while she was in Paris for the recent G7 meeting. She offered her thoughts on the diplomatic moves surrounding Ukraine, transatlantic relations, EU enlargement and a headscarf ban in Austrian schools that has caused disquiet. We also talked about the thorny negotiations involved in the EU’s next long-term budget: the Multiannual Financial Framework.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ec2d102-e355-11f1-9179-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-CLAUDIA-BAUER-TALKING-EUROPE-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ec2d102-e355-11f1-9179-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-CLAUDIA-BAUER-TALKING-EUROPE-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cc86b92a-e1a8-11f1-864d-8d7f3ec53496</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:53:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Spain’s political crossroads, Europe’s wider stakes: Spaniards to vote in key election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-spains-political-crossroads-europes-wider-stakes-spaniards-to-vote-in-key-election</link><description>
The stakes are high – not only for people in Spain, but also for Europe. On November 29, the country holds a parliamentary election that could see the end of the Socialist-led government and potentially a coalition between the right and the far right, in one of the EU’s biggest and most influential member states. It could also signal the end of Pedro Sanchez’s third term in office. Among other things, the prime minister may pay the political price for two shocking train crashes and the migrant crisis in Spain’s North African exclave of Ceuta. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb70dc0a-e434-11f1-8bdf-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/TALKING-EUROPE-SPAIN-DEBATE.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb70dc0a-e434-11f1-8bdf-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/TALKING-EUROPE-SPAIN-DEBATE.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64fa5a54-e1a9-11f1-b476-43a8f9a2efe8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:17:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>Does staggered consent actually protect young people?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261120-does-staggered-consent-actually-protect-young-people</link><description>
Following recent scandals involving two iconic British comedians, the UK government is considering the introduction of staggered age consent. Annette Young talks to Katherine Allen from the Institute of Social Justice and Crime in the UK about whether such laws work. Also the social costs of femicide; how do loved ones cope with such a loss, and what support is available to families in the wake of such a tragedy? Plus we meet the women who are challenging the traditions of Mexican mariachi music, a world that remains largely male dominated. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75df6f36-e4e6-11f1-8b81-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75df6f36-e4e6-11f1-8b81-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3cd92630-e4ca-11f1-a1e0-39177940782c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:14:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Poland slams Russian 'provocation' as missiles land near European military drills</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-poland-says-russian-missile-hit-its-territory-during-attack-on-ukraine</link><description>
Two Russian missiles and a suspected drone came down in Poland on Friday in what Prime Minister Donald Tusk said was likely an "intentional provocation" timed to coincide with European military exercises in the country for a possible postwar mission in Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0215cd4e-e4cc-11f1-ba35-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T091417Z-724863669-RC2KROAVQTVB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-POLAND-OBJECTS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0215cd4e-e4cc-11f1-ba35-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T091417Z-724863669-RC2KROAVQTVB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-POLAND-OBJECTS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a2669722-e4c9-11f1-a9b0-77b31efc897d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:38:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0215cd4e-e4cc-11f1-ba35-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T091417Z-724863669-RC2KROAVQTVB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-POLAND-OBJECTS.jpg">© Kacper Pempel, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Young people across Europe stage mass 'fight for our future' protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-europe-s-youth-set-to-join-mass-cost-of-living-protests-in-25-countries</link><description>
A fresh wave of student protests took place across Europe Friday, inspired by demonstrations that have rocked France for weeks. Their demands range from more funding for education to climate justice and even ending conscription. Further youth protests are set to take place across the continent over the weekend.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c479d6d8-e4b7-11f1-9b6e-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321479139816.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c479d6d8-e4b7-11f1-9b6e-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321479139816.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb122d10-e4b7-11f1-9b30-8f0cacea5e64</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:57:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c479d6d8-e4b7-11f1-9b6e-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321479139816.jpg">© Aurelien Morissard, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>France seeks UN Security Council meeting after Russian strikes hit European embassies in Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says</link><description>
France called for a UN Security Council meeting following a salvo of Russian strikes on Ukraine Friday that damaged the Austrian and Dutch embassies in Kyiv, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said. The new wave of missile and drone attacks came after Russian President Vladimir Putin vowed a "painful" response to Ukraine's strike on a bridge that links occupied Crimea with the Russian mainland. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc4e63e4-e4c5-11f1-bd73-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T090314Z-647512984-RC2LROAKCHGW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc4e63e4-e4c5-11f1-bd73-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T090314Z-647512984-RC2LROAKCHGW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c85c9ea-e4ab-11f1-a114-d3a799165f5c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:32:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc4e63e4-e4c5-11f1-bd73-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T090314Z-647512984-RC2LROAKCHGW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Thomas Peter, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Czechs protest en masse against growing concentration of power, threats to press freedom</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-czechs-protest-en-masse-against-concentration-of-power-in-one-hand-and-growing-control-over-media</link><description>
As large demonstrations in the Czech Republic challenge Prime Minister Andrej Babiš's plans to change the funding model of public broadcasters, Chair of the Million Moments for Democracy movement Mikuláš Minář joins François Picard from Prague for Spotlight, warning that his country risks following Hungary and Slovakia in democratic backsliding. "We are really afraid that the Czech Republic is following the Orbánian Hungarian way, (Fico's) Slovakian way," he says.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a816a9a-e4a7-11f1-87a2-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e133a2a8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a816a9a-e4a7-11f1-87a2-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e133a2a8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f8a83266-e4a7-11f1-b6fc-0f49ce47132d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:02:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Burnham hails 'landmark' EU-UK deal on trade, youth mobility as 'good day' for Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-eu-and-uk-set-to-sign-deals-on-trade-energy-youth-mobility-at-brussels-summit</link><description>
The United Kingdom and European Union agreed to a new deal on trade, energy and youth mobility on Friday, which UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham called a "good day" for both London and the bloc. Burnham – who has said he hopes to see Britain rejoin the EU in his lifetime – argues the deals will help fix some of the damage Brexit inflicted.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdbd676e-e4e6-11f1-937b-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132734Z-1827993248-RC2OROAYAMFA-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT-BURNHAM.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdbd676e-e4e6-11f1-937b-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132734Z-1827993248-RC2OROAYAMFA-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT-BURNHAM.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">215366b2-e486-11f1-8392-c54bec5a97cd</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:00:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdbd676e-e4e6-11f1-937b-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132734Z-1827993248-RC2OROAYAMFA-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT-BURNHAM.jpg">© Hannah McKay, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
